\section{Account and token}{

Create a \href{https://account.mapbox.com/auth/signup/}{Mapbox account}, verify your
email, and copy your public token from the
\href{https://console.mapbox.com/account/access-tokens/}{Access Tokens page}.
A public token begins with \code{pk.}. The provided token can be used for local
experimentation.
}

\section{R setup}{

Install the optional \code{mapgl} package. Add the following line to your user
\code{.Renviron} file, replacing the placeholder with your own token:
\preformatted{MAPBOX_PUBLIC_TOKEN="pk.YOUR_PUBLIC_TOKEN"}
Restart R afterward. Check \code{nzchar(Sys.getenv("MAPBOX_PUBLIC_TOKEN"))}:
\code{TRUE} confirms presence without printing the token. If available,
\code{usethis::edit_r_environ()} opens the file; this helper is optional. See the
\href{https://walker-data.com/mapgl/articles/getting-started.html}{mapgl setup guide}.

Public tokens are visible in rendered browser widgets. For production, use a
dedicated public token with the necessary read scopes, including \code{styles:read}
and \code{fonts:read}, and appropriate URL restrictions. The default public token
cannot have URL restrictions. Restricted development tokens must allow
\code{localhost}; Mapbox recommends a separate, more permissive development token.
See \href{https://docs.mapbox.com/accounts/guides/tokens/}{token management}.
}

\section{Package website on GitHub Pages}{

The website workflow renders the interactive README examples when the
repository has an Actions secret named \code{MAPBOX_PUBLIC_TOKEN}. On GitHub, open
\strong{Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions > New repository secret}. Use
\code{MAPBOX_PUBLIC_TOKEN} for the name and your public \code{pk.} token for the value.
Then run \strong{Actions > Package website > Run workflow} on \code{main}, after the
website build changes have been merged. See GitHub's
\href{https://docs.github.com/en/actions/how-tos/write-workflows/choose-what-workflows-do/use-secrets}{secret setup instructions}.

For a dedicated website token, allow \verb{https://www.shirokuriwaki.com} in its
URL restrictions and retain the public \code{styles:read} and \code{fonts:read} scopes.
The token is embedded in the published widget HTML; storing it as a GitHub
secret keeps it out of source files but does not hide it from site visitors.
The website displays a labeled TN-09 fallback screenshot if the live map
cannot load, including token, network, or WebGL failures. A slow map can
replace the screenshot once it finishes loading. Builds without the secret,
including fork pull requests, or with rendering errors show the screenshots
directly. The GitHub README links to the live maps and keeps its labeled
screenshots collapsed because GitHub cannot display interactive widgets.

To preview locally, set \code{MAPBOX_PUBLIC_TOKEN} in R, run
\code{source(".github/scripts/build-home.R")}, then \code{pkgdown::build_site()}.
Allow \verb{http://localhost} on the development token when serving locally.
}

\section{Free usage and billing}{

The card-free trial permits \strong{5,000 GL JS map loads per month} and provides
one token with restricted token-management options. Adding a payment method
enables pay as you go: the first \strong{50,000 map loads per month} are free;
excess usage is billable. The next 50,000 loads cost $5 per 1,000. See
\href{https://docs.mapbox.com/accounts/guides/signup/}{trial limits} and
\href{https://www.mapbox.com/pricing}{current pricing}.

Each newly initialized map counts as a load. One widget containing several
Congress layers initializes one map; toggling layers, panning, and zooming do
not add loads. Reloading initializes another map. Sessions last at most
12 hours. See \href{https://docs.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/guides/pricing/}{GL JS billing}.

Monitor usage and configure email notifications in the Mapbox Console.
Notifications \strong{do not cap charges or stop service}; see the
\href{https://docs.mapbox.com/accounts/faq/can-i-set-up-a-cap-for-monthly-spending/}{billing-cap FAQ}.
}

\section{Screenshots}{

Saving a PNG from the already rendered map does not initialize another map.
Reopening the widget for a screenshot does. The
\href{https://walker-data.com/mapgl/reference/add_screenshot_control.html}{mapgl screenshot control}
retains attribution. Preserve the Mapbox logo and map attribution in shared
images; see \href{https://docs.mapbox.com/help/dive-deeper/attribution/}{attribution guidance}.
}

